            <ArticleTitle>Subacute osteomyelitis of the femur due to Fusobacterium nucleatum in a 7-year-old boy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>324-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/INF.0000000000000558</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Subacute hematogenous osteomyelitis is an insidious infection, which commonly has a delayed diagnosis. We describe the case of a 7-year-old boy with subacute osteomyelitis, which was initially considered to be a bone tumor. Infection should be considered in all cases of bone pain, especially in children, even in the absence of typical systemic features of inflammation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
